{{!-- P14C-85737: "Change Method" link, replacing the back-arrow button on
     authentication screens. Rendered when canChangeDevice is true (paired
     devices > 1, or paired == 1 with manualPairing) — computed at render time
     on the root state.

     Default form: a self-contained text-block on its own line, used by the
     screens where the IK renders the link standalone (assertion-required,
     pingid-desktop-gen2-assertion, push-confirmation-rejected, and the
     push-confirmation-timed-out retry branch).

     Inline form (inline=true): a bare anchor with margin-left, for placing on
     the same line as the device target/nickname — matching the IK templates
     that render the anchor inside the nickname text-block with
     margin-left: 8px (otp-required, push-confirmation-waiting,
     push-confirmation-timed-out OTP branch). --}}
{{#if @root.canChangeDevice}}
{{#if inline}}
<a tabindex="0" id="changeDevice" data-id="change-method-link" target="_self" class="anchor"
   style="margin-left: 8px;">
  Change Method
</a>
{{else}}
<div class="text-block" data-id="textblock">
  <div class="text-block--overflow-wrap">
    <a tabindex="0" id="changeDevice" data-id="change-method-link" target="_self" class="anchor">
      Change Method
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
